}

sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Echinarachnius parma Holocene 60 µm Schnakenberg Turing wavelength faithfully reproduces Echinarachnius parma morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Echinarachnius parma specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/echinarachnius_parma_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Echinarachnius parma; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) diffusion-driven instability at a finite wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses faster than the activator | Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v | Gierer and Meinhardt (1972) short-range activation with long-range inhibition; Kondo and Miura (2010) reaction-diffusion as a patterning framework | Seilacher (1979) constructional morphology of the sand-dollar test at centimetre scale; reconstructed_in_script: Periodic Fourier IMEX Schnakenberg integration on a 480 µm patch. Equilibrated FFT wavelength 60.336 µm; linear peak 61.343 µm; Pearson r 0.9965 across seven diffusivity scales; RMSE 2.575 µm | Equal-diffusion ablation amplitude 5.69e-3, marked on the figure. 10 µm predecessor patch amplitude 0, marked quenched | USNM E39365 split into 3 discs after a 15 px closing: mean circularity 0.730 versus union circularity 0.066; mean aspect 0.994 versus union aspect 1.413 | 71 ocellus peaks picked with a one-period window. Mean spacing 49.21 µm, CV 0.330, KS 0.415 against Normal(λ_FFT, s); transfer_boundary: Du and Dv place the lattice on the assigned 60 µm scale. They are not measured sand-dollar diffusivities. | Seilacher (1979) does not report a 60 µm pigment spacing. The chronoseries is 1/1 at 0 Ma; the predecessor and successor are the 10 µm and 600 µm scale tiers. | Nearest-neighbour distance is not the FFT period. The radial spectrum carries the wavelength law; the spacing distribution is broader (CV 0.33).; does_not_claim: A measured echinochrome diffusion constant, a pigment gene network, or a fit to the centimetre-scale petaloid | That the 49 µm nearest-neighbour mean equals the 60 µm Turing wavelength | Sibling slot 160 parameters (α = 1.71, β = 0.43)]; phenomenon_size: 68 µm (6.84e-05 m, log10=-4.165 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 68 µm to 10.7 cm): 68 µm:echinarachnius-parma-bioelectric-polarity, 240 µm:echinarachnius-parma-vertex-packing, 2.4 mm:echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength, 4.3 mm:echinarachnius-parma-clock-wavefront, 1.4 cm:echinarachnius-parma-morphogen-condensation, 1.9 cm:echinarachnius-parma-flux-canalization, 2.0 cm:echinarachnius-parma-elastic-buckling, 2.4 cm:echinarachnius-parma-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0094837300006527>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

